<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-McIntosh says ING position unclear.</title>
<headline>RTRS-McIntosh says ING position unclear.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>McIntosh Securities Ltd chairman John McIntosh said on Tuesday the brokerage firm is unsure whether ING Bank will accept the takeover offer by Merrill Lynch and Co Inc unveiled earlier on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are of the view that ING act in a rational manner, but we are not absolutely positive what their position will be,&quot; McIntosh said at a news conference.</p>
<p>ING has a 20 percent stake in McIntosh, which has agreed to a A$117 million takeover bid by New York-based Merrill. McIntosh said he and Merrill executives spoke to ING just before the offer was announced. -- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
